{"ts": "2026-10-28T00:02:08.414888Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T0001Z-66b2", "unit": "openspec:add-pdp-cedar", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "C-b4a29f2d", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied as it stands. The tracing test builds the base request, replaces the Tool entity's effect attribute with a string of 300,000 characters, calls check, and asserts that the decision is deny, that errors deep-equals [\"PDP_REQUEST_TOO_LARGE\"] and that reasons is empty; the latest report lists it as passed. The only clause the test does not assert is the value of MAX_REQUEST_CHARS, and the repository settles that directly: values.ts exports it as 262144, and guards.ts compares the length of JSON.stringify of the context and entities against it, returning PDP_REQUEST_TOO_LARGE before the action, entity and Cedar evaluation steps, which runCheck turns into a deny with that single error and no reasons.", "text_sha256": "7aaf56173048d18a8cc30bdc332841d4c958257e3a24fbf60bcb122803e6ef94", "answer_sha256": "6459945aeaf108d3f372501fd71ed894af012dc54cee215e66bcd896201ab833", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-28T00:02:08.416237Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T0001Z-66b2", "unit": "openspec:add-pdp-cedar", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "F-2fc9e5f3", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is correct and stands. design.md § Test plan defines M8 as permit (principal, action == Action::\"reed\", resource);, an unknown action in the action scope, and the scenario \"Each malformed policy is refused\" says each of M1 to M8 of design.md is loaded as the only policy of source m-src and rejected with PDP_POLICY_INVALID, stage validate and ids [\"bad\"]. The M8 entry of the malformed-policy test instead loads @id(\"bad\") permit (principal, action == Action::\"read\", resource == Action::\"reed\");, which keeps the declared action read and puts an action entity in the resource slot. That is a different validation fault, so the unknown-action case the design names is never exercised, and the later add-policy-catalogue change relies on exactly that case being refused at stage validate with the policy id. The fix is to replace the M8 text with the design's text; the other entries M1 to M7 already match design.md word for word. WHEN the only policy of source m-src is @id(\"bad\") permi", "text_sha256": "04a5e0c4c3a1e2b62e2a1bdf86ff98fa05a4bec611b6ad8e10da2207b4a306ec", "answer_sha256": "b7aab65bc89520e03faa726c6907071f3feaeec0a303e79d087b28f176868303", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
